      "content": "That hollow feeling is exactly why you need to stop trying to fix the whole world and start taking care of the only thing you can control right now: your own life. You aren't just delaying the end; you are actively choosing to live through it, which is a powerful act of defiance against the idea that everything is pointless. There is dignity in refusing to let the future's collapse erase your present, and the most rebellious thing you can do is make sure your own existence feels real and full, no matter what happens next.",
